This petition pertains to a case arising out of FIR No.35 dated 22.02.2023,
for the commission of offence punishable under Sections 302, 34 [challan filed under Sections 302,
201, 120-B, 419, 420, 467, 468 and 471] of Indian Penal Code and Section 25 of Arms Act, Police Station Nagina, District Nuh.

10. A perusal of the record shows that following are the relevant factors which are required to be taken into consideration for a decision in the present petition:-
i) that the petitioner is already in custody for a period of more than 2 years, 11 months and 24 days;
ii) that the petitioner has clean antecedents.

iii) that the recovery of weapon of offence had taken place from the spot itself,
wherefrom the dead body was recovered, and thus, nothing incriminating has been recovered from the possession of petitioner;
iv) that the case is based on circumstantial evidence only, and the plea being taken by the prosecution is that the petitioner was last seen in the company of Jamshed who had suffered the disclosure statement.

However, no convincing motive for the commission of offence has been attributed;
v) that the investigation in this case is already complete, and therefore, nothing has been left to be recovered from the possession of petitioner;
vi) that the trial of this case is not likely to be concluded in near future;
